      "writtenOn": "2020-04-03T21:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, do you mean the +1?  That\u0027s just taking advantage of the ordering of the VDM commands for now, not the long-term plan.  It should be removed by the time the alternate mode re-vamp is done.  I can call that out in a comment.\n\nCurrently, vdm_cmd tracks where we are in the process with the last VDM sent, and it happens that we walk down the enum as we go (discover identity -\u003e discover SVID -\u003e discover mode -\u003e enter mode).  I\u0027ve found it\u0027s a bit more resilient to things like interruptions than the v1 stack, which always relied on the incoming message type to continue on its merry way.",
